      "content": "I hear you, but if we follow your advice and alienate a huge chunk of our current revenue, we might not even be around long enough to see that \"long-term\" shift you're talking about. If the board sees this as prioritizing ideology over shareholder value, it's going to be a mess. Just to be clear, you're saying the most \"logical\" business decision is to take a side even if it causes immediate, massive financial loss? Is there really no way to frame neutrality as a strategic move rather than just being \"passive\"?",
